WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:02.110
In the present time,

00:02.650 --> 00:05.900
with VR headgear,
you can go into a virtual world

00:05.900 --> 00:09.000
and play as the resident of that world.

00:09.570 --> 00:13.790
VR Full-Dive games are
at the height of their popularity.

00:14.870 --> 00:17.830
And there exists

00:17.830 --> 00:21.960
a god-tier game that stands
above all other games

00:21.960 --> 00:24.630
with over thirty million
players worldwide.

00:24.630 --> 00:26.380
And the name of that game is...

00:26.840 --> 00:29.170
Shangri-La Frontier.

00:50.150 --> 00:56.120
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:05.270 --> 02:06.020
#34: LET THE IMPATIENCE FUEL YOU

02:06.020 --> 02:08.650
#34: LET THE IMPATIENCE FUEL YOU
Wh-What?!

02:08.650 --> 02:10.530
#34: LET THE IMPATIENCE FUEL YOU
There's another player—

02:10.530 --> 02:13.110
Pioneer in the Palace of Rabitz?!

02:13.110 --> 02:14.150
Yessir!

02:15.570 --> 02:18.950
I came across a quite
amazing human recognized

02:18.950 --> 02:21.950
by the Golden Dragon King Seigwurm,
in fact.

02:21.950 --> 02:25.500
Big brother Ceecruce told me so.

02:25.500 --> 02:28.650
Seigwurm? That's a Unique Monster, right?

02:29.420 --> 02:32.490
And yet another sibling of Emul...

02:33.650 --> 02:37.260
So there's another player who triggered
the insanely difficult requirement

02:37.260 --> 02:44.100
and accepted the Invitation from Rabitz
Unique Scenario beside me.

02:44.770 --> 02:46.190
Which means...

02:48.190 --> 02:53.530
There is a high chance that player will get
to the Vorpal Epic EX Unique Scenario

02:53.530 --> 02:57.740
that I currently have a monopoly on!

02:57.740 --> 03:02.500
This is bad! This is really bad!

03:03.160 --> 03:07.000
You sure are full of energy right
after you're back, Mr. Sunraku.

03:07.500 --> 03:11.340
It was an advantage because
nobody else knew about it.

03:11.880 --> 03:16.340
If word about Invitation to Rabitz
gets spread on the internet...

03:16.340 --> 03:21.140
The Wolf-Gang's...
No, my edge will disappear!

03:22.390 --> 03:26.440
I've already got a hot potato with
the name SF-Zoo to deal with.

03:26.440 --> 03:29.940
If people find out about that
Rabitz EX Unique Scenario...

03:29.940 --> 03:34.780
Schwarz Vulf and the Library
will butt in and make things worse!

03:35.510 --> 03:37.240
Should I consult this with Pencilgon?

03:37.240 --> 03:39.530
No, there's no time.

03:39.530 --> 03:43.910
I promised to go to Fifticia
by 8 AM tomorrow morning

03:43.910 --> 03:47.480
and meet up with Rust and Mordo.

03:48.000 --> 03:51.920
That said, I can't exactly ditch them.

03:57.760 --> 03:59.300
Mr. Sunraku?

04:01.260 --> 04:05.020
Argh! My mind's rolling
left and right to no end!

04:05.430 --> 04:10.610
Emul! Do you know the name of
that other player— I mean, Pioneer?

04:10.610 --> 04:14.860
Puhh mee drnn ffrrst!

04:14.860 --> 04:16.420
Huh? What?

04:16.420 --> 04:18.570
Aghkisuakahne...

04:18.570 --> 04:19.450
Huh?

04:23.410 --> 04:25.040
Umm...

04:25.360 --> 04:28.540
Yes. She's quite a skilled fighter.

04:29.210 --> 04:33.040
I was hoping to introduce her
to our father...

04:33.040 --> 04:34.920
Yes, over here, please.

04:35.800 --> 04:38.300
This is my sister, Emul.

04:38.300 --> 04:40.050
Oh, right, Ceecrue.

04:42.470 --> 04:44.560
Nice to meet you, Emul.

04:48.270 --> 04:49.940
I'm Akitsuakane!

04:50.360 --> 04:51.980
She said!

04:51.980 --> 04:53.860
Akitsuakane?

04:54.440 --> 04:57.110
No, never heard of her.

04:57.110 --> 04:58.860
How could I?

04:58.860 --> 05:02.570
SLF has over thirty million players.

05:02.570 --> 05:05.120
That's like tens of thousands
of times more than BOP.

05:05.740 --> 05:11.670
Looking for one person is like looking
for an ant's contact lens in the desert.

05:12.750 --> 05:13.750
But...

05:14.380 --> 05:16.670
Maybe I can still do
something about this.

05:17.130 --> 05:19.550
What do you mean?

05:19.550 --> 05:22.430
I'd like to meet that
"Akitsuakane" person.

05:22.430 --> 05:24.430
Is she still at the palace?

05:24.430 --> 05:26.180
Since she's looking for Dad—

05:26.180 --> 05:29.560
I mean, Boss, she said she'd
be resting until he's back.

05:29.560 --> 05:31.770
So she's logged out...

05:31.770 --> 05:34.060
How about your brother Ceecrue
who took her in?

05:34.730 --> 05:38.820
He tends to disappear from
time to time, so I don't know.

05:39.210 --> 05:41.900
Tch, talk about bad timing.

05:41.900 --> 05:44.240
No, calm down.

05:44.240 --> 05:46.410
This is basically an RNG.

05:46.990 --> 05:50.580
I'll have to bet on the chances
that this "Akitsuakane" player

05:50.580 --> 05:53.670
won't spread a word about all this.

05:53.670 --> 05:55.290
RNG

05:57.300 --> 06:00.840
It's no use. I have no good
memories of playing with RNG.

06:00.840 --> 06:02.800
What is "RNG"?

06:02.800 --> 06:04.680
It's the rule of the world.

06:08.760 --> 06:14.650
Anyway, what I need to do now
is to head to Fifticia.

06:15.310 --> 06:19.400
First, I go from the Ruins
of Past Glories to Leventar...

06:19.400 --> 06:24.410
And then,
beyond the Barren Darkruin is Fifticia.

06:24.410 --> 06:26.490
It's quite a long trip.

06:26.490 --> 06:29.370
Can I make it by 8 AM tomorrow?

06:30.270 --> 06:33.000
It's been a while since
we hit the road. I can't wait!

06:33.000 --> 06:36.250
Uhh, sorry, but I can't take you with me.

06:36.250 --> 06:37.290
What?!

06:37.290 --> 06:41.420
Why is that?! You've been leaving me
behind way too much lately!

06:43.800 --> 06:48.510
That's because I've got an incredibly
important mission for you to do!

06:48.510 --> 06:52.350
An important mission?!
Of grave importance?!

06:52.350 --> 06:53.600
Indeed!

06:53.600 --> 06:59.150
Akitsuakane should come back to
the Palace of Rabitz to see Boss Vash.

06:59.150 --> 07:00.860
And when she does, Emul!

07:03.900 --> 07:09.870
I want you to either report back to me
or hold her in place for me!

07:10.230 --> 07:12.320
I don't really understand,

07:12.320 --> 07:15.120
but you want me to wait
for her in Rabitz, yes?

07:15.120 --> 07:17.750
That's right! I'm counting on ya!

07:17.750 --> 07:19.540
I'll try my best!

07:21.800 --> 07:26.510
Works every time. But she's so easy to trick
that I feel kinda worried for her.

07:27.220 --> 07:29.720
Now, set up a gate to
Eighthold for me, will ya?

07:29.720 --> 07:30.850
Yessir!

07:30.850 --> 07:33.140
I was wondering what
caused all the ruckus,

07:33.140 --> 07:35.100
but the bird guy is back, eh?

07:35.980 --> 07:37.770
Hey there, Ancient Craftsman.

07:37.770 --> 07:39.110
BigsisBee?

07:39.520 --> 07:41.900
I don't have much time,
but what's up?

07:41.900 --> 07:43.230
"What's up" my ass.

07:43.230 --> 07:44.900
I'm not giving you my carrot!

07:44.900 --> 07:46.320
I ain't asking!

07:46.780 --> 07:48.610
I finished it!

07:48.610 --> 07:49.950
What do you mean?

07:50.490 --> 07:52.540
Finished? Do you mean...

07:52.540 --> 07:58.420
Yeah! I used both the Crystal Scorpion
and Goldy Scorpion parts for 'em!

07:58.420 --> 08:01.040
It's my best work yet!

08:01.040 --> 08:04.920
Re-Legacy Weapon: Gilta Brille!

08:04.920 --> 08:07.170
RE-LEGACY WEAPON
GILTA BRILLE

08:07.170 --> 08:09.470
Whoa! Huge!

08:09.470 --> 08:11.680
Is this the weapon I asked you to make?!

08:12.180 --> 08:13.850
Just as ya ordered!

08:13.850 --> 08:15.180
That time...

08:15.180 --> 08:18.140
So, what do you want me to make?
A set of twinblades?

08:18.140 --> 08:19.270
Nah.

08:19.810 --> 08:23.730
I'd like to broaden my combat options.
I'll go with that instead.

08:24.630 --> 08:27.360
Make me a gauntlet for combat.

08:27.360 --> 08:29.490
...and that's the result!

08:29.490 --> 08:31.950
Yeah, I sure did say that.

08:31.950 --> 08:34.410
But I wasn't anticipating
something this size.

08:34.410 --> 08:36.370
Can I even put these on my arms?

08:36.370 --> 08:39.830
Sure ya can! I oversee it
down to the last detail!

08:39.830 --> 08:43.130
And what's great is with Divinity tech,
ya can use yer voice to—

08:43.130 --> 08:46.420
Okay, cool. I'll test it
out in battle after this.

08:46.420 --> 08:49.010
Huh?! Don't you wanna
hear about the process?!

08:49.970 --> 08:52.220
Sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

08:52.220 --> 08:55.140
I'll be back to hear all that
and tell you my impressions.

08:55.140 --> 08:56.950
Save the story for then, okay?

08:56.950 --> 09:00.190
Until then, you can go ahead
and talk to Emul instead.

09:00.190 --> 09:04.270
Huh? I don't care about
that kinda stuff either.

09:04.270 --> 09:05.750
Don't worry.

09:05.750 --> 09:08.070
Just nod and compliment her randomly.

09:08.070 --> 09:10.280
Think of yourself
as an Akabeko bobblehead doll.

09:10.280 --> 09:11.740
Akabeko?

09:11.740 --> 09:13.240
You lout...

09:13.950 --> 09:18.790
Do ya have a goddamn idea
just how great those things are?!

09:24.180 --> 09:25.420
That was close.

09:27.130 --> 09:29.610
She's all yours, Emul.

09:31.880 --> 09:35.390
Now, the question is
how to get from Eighthold...

09:35.930 --> 09:39.640
...all the way to Fifticia by tomorrow.

09:42.140 --> 09:49.030
Although I'm level 99 now,
here on out is the second-half content.

09:51.610 --> 09:53.950
What does this "Extend" mean?

09:53.950 --> 09:56.660
Is it saying I can uncap it or something?

09:58.580 --> 10:00.200
I'll look into it later.

10:01.330 --> 10:04.880
Still, beyond this point
is brand-new content for me.

10:04.880 --> 10:10.760
Based on experience, I'm sure the difficulty
of playing solo will skyrocket.

10:11.550 --> 10:15.550
With the little time I have,
I'd like some assistance.

10:20.180 --> 10:24.020
Nah, I bet they'll start interrogating me
and it'll be a pain in the ass.

10:24.020 --> 10:26.230
I'll pass on them this time.

10:26.680 --> 10:29.730
As for other people I know...

10:29.730 --> 10:33.240
It's those who were at that meeting.

10:42.910 --> 10:45.620
I wonder if they could help me out.

10:47.750 --> 10:50.500
Well, no harm in inviting them at least.

10:53.010 --> 10:56.680
SCHWARZ VULF HEADQUARTER

10:58.760 --> 11:00.010
For me?

11:08.560 --> 11:09.860
From who?

11:09.860 --> 11:11.320
From Animalia.

11:11.860 --> 11:14.320
She seems to be interested in Lycagon.

11:14.740 --> 11:18.200
So that furry finally
set her eyes on Lycagon.

11:18.200 --> 11:21.580
If anything, it's we who'd like to know.

11:21.580 --> 11:25.330
She contacted me
this morning too, you know.

11:33.630 --> 11:36.470
Ah, she even hit on Psyger-0.

11:36.470 --> 11:39.550
Is she hitting up just about
anyone she knows?

11:39.550 --> 11:43.430
You guys can ignore them.
I'll send her a reply for all of you.

11:53.730 --> 11:54.690
What's wrong?

11:56.400 --> 11:59.410
I will... log out... for a moment.

12:11.710 --> 12:12.840
What's up with her?

12:12.840 --> 12:13.960
Beats me.

12:17.880 --> 12:20.390
SAIGA

12:26.100 --> 12:27.390
What should I do?

12:28.520 --> 12:30.400
F-Finally...

12:31.860 --> 12:33.860
It's finally happening.

12:34.440 --> 12:37.440
The time is finally here!

12:38.490 --> 12:45.950
Hi... Hizutome... is finally...
sending me... an invite!

12:48.460 --> 12:51.710
CONSTANT PROGRESS

12:56.710 --> 12:59.680
What?! They logged out?!

12:59.680 --> 13:02.010
Did I send them at a bad timing?

13:02.010 --> 13:04.970
I don't have anyone else
to turn to, though.

13:07.470 --> 13:09.980
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

13:10.980 --> 13:13.730
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

13:16.940 --> 13:18.990
What the heck?!

13:21.490 --> 13:22.740
CANNOT EQUIP DUE TO INSUFFICIENT STATS

13:25.990 --> 13:28.910
I need 300 vitality?!

13:28.910 --> 13:31.040
Yet another thing I can't equip?!

13:31.040 --> 13:33.250
I'm sick of this!

13:33.250 --> 13:35.250
Goddammit!

13:35.250 --> 13:37.530
Reading the description
text of this Gilta Brille,

13:37.530 --> 13:40.800
it's packed with a hell
lot of neat features, too!

13:41.970 --> 13:45.890
Wait, I can raise my vitality
with equipment, right?

13:48.640 --> 13:51.140
This repaired Spiked Battlehelm...

13:51.140 --> 13:54.230
The vitality it gives me...

13:54.230 --> 13:57.190
SPIKED BATTLEHELM [4A] VITALITY +500
Yep! Plus 500!

13:57.190 --> 14:04.070
Ta-dah! By equipping this,
I can easily equip Gilta Brille!

14:04.070 --> 14:07.870
Vitality didn't mean a thing
in the Wethermon fight,

14:07.870 --> 14:10.580
so I only focused on
its head-parry ability,

14:10.580 --> 14:13.580
but it's got tons of vitality!

14:13.580 --> 14:16.960
Man, I'm glad I had this made.

14:16.960 --> 14:19.630
I owe Beelach a big time for this.

14:19.630 --> 14:21.090
What a busy fella.

14:21.590 --> 14:26.180
Now I just have to assign my leftover
points to my strength and tech.

14:27.300 --> 14:30.600
And I can use the help as
a kind of "transformation"

14:30.600 --> 14:33.060
when I want to use the Gilta Brille.

14:41.740 --> 14:43.900
A reply from Psyger-0?

14:43.900 --> 14:48.200
My sincerest apology for this late reply.

14:48.700 --> 14:51.580
First, thank you very much
for inviting me.

14:52.120 --> 14:54.710
I'd be delighted to accompany you.

14:55.210 --> 14:57.420
Now as for our meeting spot—

14:58.790 --> 15:03.970
They're still as formal as ever,
but sounds like they'll help me out.

15:03.970 --> 15:05.930
Great! I appreciate that!

15:05.930 --> 15:11.680
So we will meet up
in the eleventh town, Leventar.

15:13.060 --> 15:16.650
Which is right past this
"Ruins of Past Glories."

15:18.310 --> 15:22.190
If I'm gonna arrive at Fifticia
by 8 AM tomorrow

15:22.190 --> 15:23.940
to meet up with Rust and Mordo,

15:24.360 --> 15:28.410
I'll need to meet up with Psyger-0
and get going from there.

15:29.200 --> 15:32.490
All right. It's a race against time.

15:34.620 --> 15:37.250
Let's go beat the area boss right away!

15:39.500 --> 15:43.210
To get to Fifticia,
where I'll meet Rust and Mordo,

15:43.210 --> 15:45.260
I looked up a bunch of stuff online.

15:45.880 --> 15:47.720
THIRDREMA → FOURFOLKSHIRE ROUTE,
Apparently in SLF,

15:47.720 --> 15:50.050
THIRDREMA → FOURFOLKSHIRE ROUTE,
the path from Thirdrema to Fifticia

15:50.050 --> 15:53.310
FIVELLE ROUTE, SIXENVELDT ROUTE → FIFTICIA
splits into three routes in general.

15:53.310 --> 15:54.270
FIVELLE ROUTE, SIXENVELDT ROUTE → FIFTICIA

15:54.270 --> 15:59.900
That explains why there are three areas
you can access after exiting Thirdrema.

16:00.610 --> 16:03.190
This route I'm taking
that goes past Fourfolkshire

16:03.190 --> 16:08.660
is the choice of most people
because it's the simplest, straight route.

16:09.240 --> 16:11.160
And one reason for that...

16:11.740 --> 16:16.580
...lies in the Area Boss in this
Ruins of Past Glories.

16:23.460 --> 16:27.050
Oops, looks like I'm finally here, eh?

16:29.340 --> 16:32.100
I've done my research on you,

16:32.640 --> 16:34.140
Area Boss!

16:36.640 --> 16:39.440
The Area Boss of the Ruins of Past Glories.

16:39.940 --> 16:46.820
Its body composed of junk and rubble
changes its traits at random,

16:46.820 --> 16:50.360
and cycles through a slew
of effective attacks.

16:51.070 --> 16:56.830
What's more, as the rubble covering its body
also serves as a sturdy armor coating,

16:56.830 --> 16:59.000
it's hard to deal damage to it.

16:59.540 --> 17:02.670
It's a gigantic boss fitting
for the game's second half.

17:14.930 --> 17:17.390
AREA BOSS
OVERDRESS GOLEM

17:17.390 --> 17:20.140
Overdress Golem...

17:20.140 --> 17:22.650
I heard it was huge...

17:23.080 --> 17:26.820
...but this is practically a mountain!

17:29.280 --> 17:31.530
But I know your secret.

17:31.900 --> 17:36.030
You used to be a force to be feared,
but ever since your weakness was found,

17:36.400 --> 17:41.370
you're now nothing more than
veteran players' speedrun punching bag.

17:42.460 --> 17:45.670
The record beat time was one minute.

17:46.170 --> 17:49.920
Let's renew that record!
I'm breakin' a minute today!

17:51.050 --> 17:52.180
NITROGAIN - IGNITION - CLIMAX BOOST

17:54.430 --> 17:56.140
Skate Foot!

17:58.060 --> 18:01.390
First I'll sneak behind its back
and climb up!

18:04.020 --> 18:07.440
The evolved version of
the Vorpal Blade Art Mirror Reflection!

18:07.440 --> 18:08.980
Vorpal Secret Arts!

18:09.780 --> 18:10.570
Mirror of Fading!

18:10.570 --> 18:11.610
VORPAL SECRET ARTS: MIRROR OF FADING
Mirror of Fading!

18:11.610 --> 18:13.530
VORPAL SECRET ARTS: MIRROR OF FADING

18:21.750 --> 18:25.080
Instead of directing the enemy's target
to behind my back,

18:25.080 --> 18:27.500
this skill let me leave
a projection behind!

18:28.630 --> 18:32.590
Basically, I can make a decoy of myself
for a few seconds!

18:33.220 --> 18:36.720
Normally a tank would grab
the enemy's attention,

18:37.130 --> 18:39.720
but now I can do it myself!

18:40.060 --> 18:42.230
And evolved from Boat Leap!

18:45.230 --> 18:46.900
Shana-oh Possession!

18:46.900 --> 18:48.650
SHANA-OH POSSESSION

18:48.650 --> 18:53.570
Unlike the Boat Leaps that only offered
a limited number of buffed jumps,

18:53.570 --> 18:58.410
this keeps all my jumps buffed
for 30 seconds!

18:59.740 --> 19:04.250
A path of junk...
"Ruins of Past Glories" indeed!

19:05.580 --> 19:08.170
Tch, my decoy's come apart.

19:11.300 --> 19:15.760
Heh! If there's no platform,
I can just step on thin air.

19:16.630 --> 19:18.890
The evolved form of Sky Walker!

19:18.890 --> 19:20.850
Fleet Float!

19:20.850 --> 19:23.270
FLEET FLOAT

19:25.270 --> 19:28.020
C'mon! I'm still going up and up!

19:29.230 --> 19:31.360
Great of Climb!

19:31.360 --> 19:31.860
GREAT OF CLIMB
Great of Climb!

19:31.860 --> 19:34.280
GREAT OF CLIMB

19:41.990 --> 19:46.000
I've finally made it, all the way
to the giant machine I look for!

19:46.750 --> 19:49.500
Many players have verified

19:49.500 --> 19:53.840
that the two columns supporting
the wheel are breakable.

19:54.510 --> 19:58.970
Once destroyed, the wheel will
fall following the physics engine.

19:59.510 --> 20:03.390
And it'll fall straight on
the Overdress Golem's head.

20:03.390 --> 20:05.520
That's its weakness!

20:05.940 --> 20:09.940
Up until now, I could never pull off
a destruction on this scale...

20:11.860 --> 20:15.320
But with this sweet thing,
I can break it in less than a minute!

20:16.190 --> 20:20.190
Let's beat the hell out
of its head, Gilta Brille!

20:20.950 --> 20:25.450
I can't be late for my meet-up
with Psyger-0, after all.

22:11.980 --> 22:15.730
There's still an hour before
the time we promised to meet,

22:15.730 --> 22:17.020
but I came anyway!

22:17.480 --> 22:20.240
I can't wait!

22:28.870 --> 22:31.830
SLF Theater!

22:31.830 --> 22:32.540
#36 SAINT'S HOLY WATER

22:32.540 --> 22:34.210
#36 SAINT'S HOLY WATER
Mini!

22:34.210 --> 22:35.250
#36 SAINT'S HOLY WATER

22:36.290 --> 22:38.460
Eristella, Saint of Love.

22:38.970 --> 22:41.050
The time has finally come.

22:41.550 --> 22:42.590
That's right.

22:43.010 --> 22:47.470
I've gathered money through various means,
even robbing from others.

22:47.470 --> 22:50.020
But I've finally gathered enough.

22:50.930 --> 22:54.810
Yes, because I PK'ed
my friend out of impulse,

22:54.810 --> 22:57.020
I couldn't obtain it
through legitimate means,

22:57.020 --> 22:59.820
so I intentionally stopped
my progress on the main scenario

22:59.820 --> 23:01.940
and focused on only gathering money.

23:03.400 --> 23:06.530
All to obtain your sacred holy water!

23:06.910 --> 23:10.870
With this, I'll buy your holy water,
the saint's holy water!

23:10.870 --> 23:15.170
The second chapter of my life
will finally begin!

23:17.040 --> 23:22.050
"SO BEGINS, THE SECOND CHAPTER OF HIS LIFE"

23:24.050 --> 23:25.720
Thank you for your patronage.

23:26.720 --> 23:30.810
Man, I buy up all of
